    "source": "hn",
    "title": "NariQ: BF16-level Qwen3.8-27B in a 10 GB file",
    "points": 36,
    "num_comments": 4,
    "url": "https://huggingface.co/nari-labs/Qwen3.8-27B-NariQ-GGUF",
    "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50611402",
    "created_at": "2026-11-23T13:42:38+00:00",
    "story_text": "We built NariQ: 3-bit-or-lower quantizations of Qwen3.8-27B that retain near-BF16 quality across agentic tasks, math, multilingual reasoning, and image understanding.<p>To our knowledge, this is the first 3-bit-or-lower quantization that retains BF16 lvl performance on long-horizon agentic tasks.<p>Benchmarks (BF16 &#x2F; 3-bit &#x2F; 2.5-bit &#x2F; 2-bit):<p>- DeepSWE: 39.8 &#x2F; 41.0 &#x2F; 41.9 &#x2F; 28.6<p>- Terminal-Bench 2.1: 62.6 &#x2F; 63.8 &#x2F; 60.2 &#x2F; 52.4<p>- AIME 25+26: 97.7 &#x2F; 98.3 &#x2F; 96.5 &#x2F; 86.0<p>- MSGM: 94.0 &#x2F; 93.1 &#x2F; 91.8 &#x2F; 90.6<p>- RealWorldQA: 82.4 &#x2F; 82.4 &#x2F; 81.3 &#x2F; 80.9<p>Decode speed is comparable to other quants on an RTX PRO 6000. Context-length results below<p>(3-bit &#x2F; 2.5-bit &#x2F; 2-bit &#x2F; Unsloth UD-IQ3_XXS):<p>- 4K: 88.9 &#x2F; 99.2 &#x2F; 111.7 &#x2F; 94.7<p>- 16K: 84.5 &#x2F; 93.8 &#x2F; 105.1 &#x2F; 89.8<p>- 64K: 70.7 &#x2F; 77.5 &#x2F; 85.0 &#x2F; 74.8<p>Running these currently require our llama.cpp fork:\n(<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;nari-labs&#x2F;nari-llama.cpp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;nari-labs&#x2F;nari-llama.cpp</a>)<p>Feedback and questions welcome. We&#x27;d love to hear how these perform on your workloads.",
    "matched_keywords": []
  },
